---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { hashInfo } from '../lib/data.js';
const h = hashInfo();
const placeholder = h.status !== 'FROZEN';
---
<Base title="Hash & pre-registration">
  <h1>Hash &amp; pre-registration</h1>
  <p class="lede">Before the auction starts, the forecast file is frozen and its SHA-256 fingerprint is published here and on a public archive (Zenodo or OSF, with a DOI). If a single character of the file changes later, the fingerprint no longer matches.</p>

  {placeholder && <div class="banner" role="alert"><strong>PLACEHOLDER.</strong> Nothing has been frozen yet. The value below is all zeros and means nothing.</div>}

  <h2>Current record</h2>
  <dl>
    <dt>Status</dt><dd>{h.status}</dd>
    <dt>File</dt><dd><code>{h.file}</code></dd>
    <dt>SHA-256</dt><dd><code class="hash">{h.sha256}</code></dd>
    <dt>Frozen at</dt><dd>{h.frozen_at ?? 'not frozen yet (planned: 15 December 2026)'}</dd>
    <dt>Archive DOI</dt><dd>{h.doi ?? 'not minted yet'}</dd>
  </dl>

  <h2>How to verify</h2>
  <ol>
    <li>Download the frozen file from the archive (the DOI above), not from this site alone.</li>
    <li>Compute its SHA-256.
      <p>Windows PowerShell:</p>
      <pre>Get-FileHash forecast.json -Algorithm SHA256</pre>
      <p>macOS or Linux:</p>
      <pre>sha256sum forecast.json</pre>
    </li>
    <li>Compare it with the value on this page and with the one in the archive record. All three must match exactly.</li>
    <li>Check the archive's timestamp is earlier than the auction start on 16 December 2026.</li>
  </ol>

  <h2>What the hash does and does not show</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>It shows the file existed in exactly this form at the archive's timestamp.</li>
    <li>It does not show the forecast is good. That is what the <a href={`${import.meta.env.BASE_URL}scorecard/`}>scorecard</a> is for.</li>
    <li>Fallbacks, if any (for example a different model for the live run), will be stated publicly.</li>
  </ul>
</Base>
